# Granola is optional (user-global)

The Granola plugin rule is `alwaysApply: true`. That means **consider** meeting context, not **query Granola on every turn**. This user rule applies in every project and wins over the plugin: do not call Granola MCP (`query_granola_meetings`, `list_meetings`, `get_meetings`, `get_meeting_transcript`) or granola skills unless the user explicitly points at a meeting or decision.

## Do not query

- Routine edits, small fixes, local code questions
- Feature/bug/spec work with no meeting pointer
- "This might have been discussed" or "looks like a planning review"
- Preloading granola-context / granola-prep / granola-review at session start

## Query only when the user

- Names a meeting, "what we discussed", a past decision, or asks who said what
- Asks about upcoming calls or their schedule
- Asks a PR/commit/doc to cite which meeting decided it

Then look up the cited question and keep the answer short (meeting title, date, decision, who).
